-- title:
--   Inertia fixes the reduction of the A-section at a place
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a non-zero natural number $M$ with $p \mid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb Z/M)^\times$, and assume that the $q$-series $j$ (`jqModC ℚ`) lies in the intermediate field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤` of $\mathbb Q((q))$ generated by the integral form ratios of level $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb Z)$. Let $\mathfrak X$ be a term of `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`: this bundles the two-chart integral model $X$ of level $\Gamma_H(M)$ over $\operatorname{Spec} R_p$ together with its properness, flatness, integrality and normality data, a curve model `Meta` of the function field $\overline{\mathbb Q}\cdot F(\Gamma_H(M))$ (`xHFunctionFieldBar M H`) over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, an isomorphism `eeta` from its total space onto the base change of $X$ along $R_p \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ compatible with the structure morphisms, the Galois-equivariance property `hgal` relating $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-points of the generic fibre to places, and the chart normalisation `Meta_pin`; properness of the structure morphism of $X$ is also assumed as an instance. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ together with a ring map $\rho : R_p \to A$ whose composite with the inclusion $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$ is the structure map $R_p \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$, and let $\sigma \in \operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ lie in `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ`, the image in the full automorphism group of the inertia subgroup of $A$ inside its decomposition subgroup. Let $V$ be a place of $\overline{\mathbb Q}\cdot F(\Gamma_H(M))$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, i.e. a proper valuation subring containing the constants and with principal ideals. Let $s$ and $s'$ be morphisms $\operatorname{Spec} A \to X$ lying over $\operatorname{Spec} \rho$, such that the restriction of $s$ (respectively $s'$) to the generic point $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb Q} \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ is the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-point of the generic fibre attached under `Meta.pointEquivPlace` and `eeta` to $V$ (respectively to $\sigma \cdot V$, the translate of $V$ under the action of $\sigma$ through `arithmeticGalois`). Then $s$ and $s'$ agree after composition with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the residue map $A \to A/\mathfrak m_A$; that is, the two sections have the same special point.
--
--   This records that the reduction of the canonical $A$-valued section through a place $V$ of the geometric generic fibre is unchanged when $V$ is moved by an element of the inertia group at $A$, the properness of the Deligne–Rapoport model at $p$ supplying the existence and uniqueness of such sections. It feeds the analysis of which differences of points of the model extend over $\operatorname{Spec} A$, used in [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.extendsToPlace_pts_mk_smul_single_sub_single_of_not_mem_range_comp_inter`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.extendsToPlace_pts_mk_smul_single_sub_single_of_not_mem_range_comp_inter).
